  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for people who understand the business process and use the system carefully. They judge you by process understanding, accuracy and clear notes.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is drawing a simple process flow and listing its records.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and SAP and ERP courses for non-IT students: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft process documents and explain system steps. Routine documentation shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Process judgment, accuracy and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to explain steps and verify; later, own process design.
  </p>

